From 342c0a9bdd868876992b9b9020865e4b2c5fba90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:41:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/43] moe cache: KV lending (GGML_MOE_KV_LEND=1, default off)
 -- the KV cache rows past the context in use hold copies of evicted experts

The main model's K/V tensors (one stream, V not transposed, no windowed KV / KV pool) are registered with the expert
cache; rows past a lend line (the next batch's n_kv padded to 8192 plus GGML_MOE_KV_LEND_MARGIN, default 16384, in steps
of 4096) are cut into victim slots.  When the arena evicts an expert of a RAM-tier table (on the main model's decode
stream), a copy goes to a victim slot and cold_ptrs[e] points at it, so the decode kernel's cold read is served from
VRAM; an admission of an expert with a victim copy fills device to device.  The RAM copy / file alias is still made, so
a victim is a disposable duplicate: dropping one points cold_ptrs back at its fallback, recomputed at drop time.
llama reports the rows each ubatch, state restore, K-shift, clear and seq park/unpark can touch; taking rows back
synchronises the device, re-points the victims there and zeroes the rows.  Fill-through re-points its experts at their
victim copies.  The verifier (GGML_MOE_VERIFY_AT) checks victim bytes and accepts a victim cold pointer only when the
slot holds that expert.  GGML_MOE_KV_LEND_LOG=1 logs each line move; moe_cache_report prints the totals.
